<title>USA: Allstate completes reinsurance unit sale.</title>
<headline>Allstate completes reinsurance unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allstate Insurance Co said Tuesday it completed the sale of its London-based reinsurance operation, Allstate Reinsurance Co Ltd, to QBE Insurance Group Ltd of Sydney, Australia.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction, first announced in September, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Allstate Reinsurance, with 1995 net written premiums of $92 million, was indirectly owned by Allstate Insurance, and reinsures risks mainly in the United Kingdom, continental Europe and the Middle East and Far East.</p>
<p>Allstate provides insurance for more than 20 million customers.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
